course: dictionary
lesson: 10574
title: Unction: holy oil and oily talk
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words have one meaning in church and another in everyday talk. Unction is one of them. In church, unction is the act of anointing someone with holy oil, as a sign of God's blessing, for example when someone is sick.
explain: Unction can also describe a way of talking. If someone speaks with unction, their words are too smooth, oily and falsely serious or polite. This is a formal word, and it is usually used to criticise. The clue is often that the speaker sounds false.
explain: «He sang it very loud, with great unction and expression; and when he had done, he sang it all over again.» Here unction means great feeling: the singer put his whole heart into it. The words around it, loud and expression, help you pick the right meaning.
fact: Unction is an uncountable noun, so you say some unction, not an unction or two unctions.
fact: «Extreme unction» was an old name for the anointing of the sick, a church sacrament in which a priest anoints a sick or dying person with oil.
fact: In the Bible, kings and priests were anointed with oil.
fact: Catholics and some other Christians believe that anointing brings God's strength and comfort.
fact: When used to criticise, unction suggests that smooth talk seems insincere.
exercise: «The priest offered unction to the sick woman.» In church, what is unction? | *The anointing of someone with holy oil, as a sign of God's blessing | A kind of thick soup | Cleaning the church floor | A loud, joyful song
exercise: A salesman speaks with too much unction, smiling and praising everything in a smooth, oily way. What does unction suggest? | Quiet, shy talk | Honest, plain speaking | Angry shouting | *Smooth, oily and falsely polite talk
exercise: «He sang it very loud, with great unction and expression.» What does unction mean in this sentence? | Being rude | Holy oil | Whispering | *Great feeling
test: Which is the church meaning of unction? | Eating a meal together | Ringing a bell to start a service | *Anointing someone with holy oil | Singing a song in a loud voice
test: Someone speaks with unction when they sound | *Too smooth, oily and falsely serious | Bored and tired | Angry and loud | Shy and nervous
exam: Mia says, «His unction made me wary, he was too smooth.» Using the clues, unction must mean | Loud singing | Holy oil | *Oily, falsely polite talk | Great joy
